§ `Section 88 -- Changes to numbering`

-- src:677 | For the purpose of making legislation easier to find, use, or understand, the Governor-General may, by Order in Council, authorise the PCO to—
-- src:678 | publish a version of any specified legislation with provisions numbered or renumbered in the manner indicated by the order; and
-- src:679 | publish a version of any other specified legislation, in the manner indicated by the order, so as to consequentially update any references in that legislation to those numbered or renumbered provisions.
-- src:680 | An order under this section is secondary legislation (see this Part for publication requirements).
#ASSERT `the Governor-General may authorise the PCO to publish a renumbered or consequentially updated version` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Governor-General may authorise the PCO to publish a renumbered or consequentially updated version` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Governor-General may authorise the PCO to publish a renumbered or consequentially updated version` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `an order under section 88 is secondary legislation` EQUALS TRUE

§ `Section 89 -- Changes to format`

-- src:682 | The Chief Parliamentary Counsel may authorise the PCO to make format changes to a version of legislation so that the format of the legislation is consistent with current drafting practice, or the format of the version of the legislation is easier to read or use according to the means used to read it, or both.
#ASSERT `the format change is within section 89` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the format change is within section 89` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the format change is within section 89` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the format change is within section 89` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 90 -- When changes take effect`

-- src:684 | For the purposes of amendments to, incorporation of, or reference to legislation that has had changes made to it under this subpart, those changes take effect as if enacted or made expressly by other legislation having effect immediately before the date on which the changes were made.
-- Changes made on 10 March 2026: an amendment taking effect on 10 March or later sees them; one taking effect on 9 March does not.
#ASSERT `the changes are treated as already enacted for an amendment, incorporation or reference taking effect on` (Date 10 3 2026) `to legislation changed on` (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the changes are treated as already enacted for an amendment, incorporation or reference taking effect on` (Date 11 3 2026) `to legislation changed on` (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the changes are treated as already enacted for an amendment, incorporation or reference taking effect on` (Date 9 3 2026) `to legislation changed on` (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 91 -- Changes to legislation to be noted on legislation website`

-- src:686 | If changes authorised by this subpart are made, the PCO must—
-- src:687 | indicate that fact in a suitable place in the legislation or otherwise on the legislation website; and
-- src:688 | outline in general terms, and in a suitable place in the legislation or otherwise on the legislation website, the changes made.
#ASSERT `the PCO must note the changes on the legislation website and outline them in general terms` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO must note the changes on the legislation website and outline them in general terms` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 94 -- Interpretation (revision Bills)`

-- src:702 | revision Bill means a Bill prepared under this subpart
#ASSERT `is a revision Bill` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is a revision Bill` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:703 | revision programme means a revision programme approved under section 95.
#ASSERT `is a revision programme` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is a revision programme` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 95 -- Three-yearly revision programme`

-- src:707 | A draft revision programme must set out—
-- src:708 | the revisions that are proposed to be started during the 3-year period; and
-- src:709 | the revisions that are expected to be enacted during that period; and
-- src:710 | the revisions on which work is expected to continue during that period.
#ASSERT `a draft revision programme must set out` `the revisions proposed to be started during the 3-year period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a draft revision programme must set out` `the revisions expected to be enacted during that period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a draft revision programme must set out` `the revisions on which work is expected to continue during that period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-29: was ``a draft revision programme must set out` `anything else` EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the rule that JUST FALSE needs the text's own words (NOTES, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING") replaced fork F11's second limb, and section 95(2) says a draft revision programme "must set out" three things and does not close the list with "only", so the answer is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `a draft revision programme must set out` `anything else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:711 | The Attorney-General must—
-- src:712 | make the draft publicly available and invite submissions on the draft from interested persons and members of the public, allowing a reasonable time for those submissions to be made; and
-- src:713 | present a revision programme to the House of Representatives as soon as practicable after it is approved by the Government.
#ASSERT `the Attorney-General has complied with section 95(3)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Attorney-General has complied with section 95(3)` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Attorney-General has complied with section 95(3)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Attorney-General has complied with section 95(3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:714 | The Attorney-General may amend, or replace, the 3-yearly revision programme if the Attorney-General complies with subsection (3) (applied as if the amendment or replacement were the draft or programme).
#ASSERT `the Attorney-General may amend or replace the revision programme` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Attorney-General may amend or replace the revision programme` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 96 -- Revision powers`

-- src:717 | A revision Bill may—
-- src:718 | revise the whole or part of 1 or more Acts, and for that purpose combine or divide Acts or parts of Acts:
-- src:719 | adopt a Title that is different from the Title or Titles of the Acts or parts of Acts revised:
-- src:720 | omit redundant and spent provisions:
-- src:721 | renumber and rearrange provisions from the Acts or parts of Acts revised:
-- src:722 | make changes in language, format, and punctuation to achieve a clear, consistent, gender-neutral, and modern style of expression, to achieve consistency with current drafting style and format, and generally to express better the spirit and meaning of the law:
-- src:723 | include new or additional purpose provisions, outline or overview provisions, examples, diagrams, graphics, flowcharts, readers’ notes, lists of defined terms, and other similar devices to aid accessibility and readability:
-- src:724 | include new or additional provisions alerting users of the revision to legislation that is not incorporated in the revision but is relevant to the subject matter of the revision:
-- src:725 | correct typographical, punctuation, and grammatical errors, and other similar errors:
-- src:726 | make consequential amendments to legislation that is not incorporated, or is incorporated only in part, in the revision:
-- src:727 | include any necessary repeals, transitional, savings, and related provisions.
-- src:728 | A revision Bill may also—
-- src:729 | make minor amendments to clarify Parliament’s intent, to resolve ambiguity, or to reconcile inconsistencies between provisions (or to do all of those things):
-- src:730 | update any monetary amount (other than an amount specified for the purpose of jurisdiction or an offence or penalty), having regard to movements in the Consumers Price Index over the relevant period, or provide for the amount to be prescribed by Order in Council:
-- src:731 | make minor amendments to update how provisions can be complied with, or operate, in a way that takes account of changes in technology if those amendments are consistent with the spirit and meaning of the law:
-- src:732 | for the purpose of enabling matters of general principle to be contained in Acts and matters of detail to be contained in secondary legislation,—
-- src:733 | omit forms, schedules, or other matters of detail from the Acts or parts of Acts revised, and instead authorise those matters to be prescribed by or under secondary legislation:
-- src:734 | include matters currently prescribed in secondary legislation made under the Acts or parts of Acts revised:
-- src:735 | make any other change that is necessary for the purpose of implementing subparagraph (i) or (ii) or that is consequential on doing so.
-- src:736 | In subsection (3)﻿(b), Consumers Price Index means the Consumers Price Index (all groups) published by Statistics New Zealand or, if that index ceases to be published, any measure certified by the Government Statistician as being equivalent to that index.
-- src:737 | A revision Bill must not change the effect of the law, except as authorised by subsection (3).
-- src:738 | The changes that may be made in a revision Bill include (without limitation) any of the changes that may be made under subpart 2.
