§ `Section 97 -- Format of revision Bill`

-- src:740 | A revision Bill must be in the form of a Bill suitable for introduction in the House of Representatives.
#ASSERT `the revision Bill is in the required form` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the revision Bill is in the required form` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:741 | A revision Bill’s explanatory note must include a statement setting out, in general terms, the inconsistencies, anomalies, discrepancies, and omissions that were identified in the course of preparing the revision, and how they have been remedied in the Bill.
#ASSERT `the explanatory note meets section 97(2)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the explanatory note meets section 97(2)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the explanatory note meets section 97(2)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:742 | A revision Bill may be structured so that it is able to be divided into 2 or more Bills.
#ASSERT `a revision Bill may be structured to be divided into 2 or more Bills` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a revision Bill may be structured to be divided into 2 or more Bills` FALSE EQUALS TRUE

§ `Section 98 -- Certification of revision Bill`

-- src:744 | For the purposes of this subpart, the certifiers are the President of the Law Commission, the Solicitor-General, a retired Judge of the High Court nominated by the Attorney-General, and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel.
#ASSERT `is a certifier` `the President of the Law Commission` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is a certifier` `the Solicitor-General` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is a certifier` `a retired Judge of the High Court nominated by the Attorney-General` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is a certifier` `a retired Judge of the High Court not nominated by the Attorney-General` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is a certifier` `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is a certifier` `anyone else` EQUALS FALSE
-- src:746 | The certifiers may certify a revision Bill if they are satisfied that—
-- src:747 | the revision powers set out in section 96 have been exercised appropriately in the preparation of the revision; and
-- src:748 | the revision Bill does not change the effect of the law, except as authorised by section 96(3).
#ASSERT `the certifiers may certify the revision Bill` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the certifiers may certify the revision Bill` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the certifiers may certify the revision Bill` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:745 | The Chief Parliamentary Counsel must submit a revision Bill to the certifiers for certification under this section.
-- src:749 | Before certifying a revision Bill, the certifiers may require the Chief Parliamentary Counsel to make whatever changes they consider necessary.
-- src:750 | When a revision Bill has been certified, the Chief Parliamentary Counsel must give the revision Bill and certificate to the Attorney-General.
#ASSERT `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel must give the revision Bill and certificate to the Attorney-General` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel must give the revision Bill and certificate to the Attorney-General` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 99 -- Amendments proposed by revision Bills`

-- src:752 | A revision Bill, as introduced, must not contain any proposed change to the effect of the law unless the amendment is authorised by section 96.
#ASSERT `a revision Bill as introduced may contain a proposed change to the effect of the law` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a revision Bill as introduced may contain a proposed change to the effect of the law` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:753 | However, nothing in this Act affects the powers of the House of Representatives to amend a revision Bill for any purpose and to pass it with amendment.
#ASSERT `this Act limits the powers of the House of Representatives to amend and pass a revision Bill` EQUALS FALSE

§ `The remaining rules of ss 86 to 100`

-- src:632 | Nothing in this section limits the authority to make changes in reliance on the application of section 38 or any other legislation.
#ASSERT `section 86 limits the authority to make changes in reliance on section 38 or any other legislation` EQUALS FALSE
-- src:706 | The Attorney-General must prepare a draft 3-yearly revision programme for each new Parliament.
#ASSERT `the Attorney-General must prepare a draft 3-yearly revision programme` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Attorney-General must prepare a draft 3-yearly revision programme` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:716 | The Chief Parliamentary Counsel must prepare revision Bills in accordance with the current revision programme and this section.
#ASSERT `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel has prepared the revision Bill as section 96(1) requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel has prepared the revision Bill as section 96(1) requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel has prepared the revision Bill as section 96(1) requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- src:755 | The PCO’s annual report under section 43 of the Public Finance Act 1989 may (without limitation) make—
-- src:756 | recommendations for the repeal of obsolete or redundant legislation or provisions of legislation, if their repeal is not suitable for inclusion in a revision; and
-- src:757 | recommendations for changes to 1 or more of the following:
-- src:758 | the revision powers set out in section 96:
-- src:759 | the powers under subpart 2:
-- src:760 | the procedure for the certification of revision Bills.
#ASSERT `the PCO's annual report may make` `a recommendation for the repeal of obsolete or redundant legislation or provisions, if their repeal is not suitable for inclusion in a revision` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO's annual report may make` `a recommendation for the repeal of obsolete legislation or provisions, if their repeal is not suitable for inclusion in a revision` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO's annual report may make` `a recommendation for the repeal of redundant legislation or provisions, if their repeal is not suitable for inclusion in a revision` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO's annual report may make` `a recommendation for a change to the revision powers set out in section 96` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO's annual report may make` `a recommendation for a change to the powers under subpart 2` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO's annual report may make` `a recommendation for a change to the procedure for the certification of revision Bills` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the PCO's annual report may make` `any other matter` EQUALS TRUE
